<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder shares up sharply again.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder shares up sharply again.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd shares rose 5.5 percent, or one rupee, to 19.50 rupees on retail buying on Thursday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares were rising sharply for the third straight day, they said.  </p>
<p>&quot;Plantations are on a roll due to good tea prices,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder shares rose 2.9 percent on Tuesday and 2.8 percent on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company processes tea leaf bought from small-scale cultivators.</p>
</text>
